      "writtenOn": "2025-07-25T19:35:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i tried that. what i discovered is that the compiler doesn\u0027t let you\ndefine a weak function and a regular function in the same compilation unit.\nso, if you\u0027re in a situation where you need to include `chipset.h` to get\nrelevant declarations and want to override those `static inline` functions,\nit\u0027s a no-go. `weak` is a linker directive.\n\ni\u0027m half tempted to deprecate `test_mockable_static_inline` since it doesn\u0027t\ndo what we want in many cases.\n\ni suspect this is why `TEST_DISABLE_INLINE_CHIPSET_IN_STATE` was implemented\nsome time ago.\ni\u0027d be OK folding that one into `TEST_DISABLE_INLINE_CHIPSET_FUNCTIONS`\nin the future.",
      "parentUuid": "dad52e05_2c3a5105",
      "revId": "1c88a6e6480d84dee4dda607b043676d1ea6eab9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
